From 279ba2a81b09b64c220d591f90c450d406aecd9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 05:01:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] nestscore: per-cell worth for room credit, and who a shut
 door shuts in

Prep for the colony score's dig ladder, before the feeding gate opens it.

cell_values(&score, &class): each part's credit spread over its cells
(chamber, niche, half the tunnel credit), crack/stray -0.5, pit -1, so the
values sum to the score and a harness can pay each cell to its cutter
(rung 4). Measured on the 28 controls: shelf cells of a comb 0.05-0.07,
worst blueprint chamber cell 0.42, a 7-row room 1.0; tunnel cells ~0.5 in
every nest. A first test comparing each nest's best cell failed because a
comb's best cell is a tunnel cell; the test now compares shelf to chamber.

nest_piece(...) -> Option<NestPiece> with .open, .cells, .holds(x, y)
(rung 3): the owner wants a closed door charged only when it shuts out
foraging or eating, so the harness must ask who is inside. door_open now
wraps it. An offline proxy for costly closures (pellet-holders above
ground) read 6.0 door-open vs 7.0 shut on the sealed colony: not specific,
because only the harness knows food from soil.

Faults put back: tunnel at full weight, niche spread over chamber cells,
every nest piece instead of the largest -- each turns a test red.
9 nestscore tests pass; clippy clean.

